      title: 'Facial contouring: a six-month judgment with late risks',
      body: 'View and Wonjin describe about 80 percent of swelling resolving in one to four weeks, with imaging checks out to six months. A Korean review of 53 patients who needed secondary surgery after cheekbone reduction found most cases were under- or over-correction and asymmetry; known complications include cheek drooping that appears only after swelling settles, malunion, nonunion and numbness. Bone revision is a second major operation, which is why this category belongs at a hospital-level provider with named anesthesiologists.',
      sourceIds: ['view-aftercare', 'wonjin-site', 'aps-malarplasty'],
